// D1774 — `x is U` where `U` is a union ALIAS that is an arm of `x`'s union. A union alias
// member is a SUBSET of the outer box's tags, never a nested box, so the test is the tag
// chain `as? U` already emits and `variantIndexOf` — one name, one variant — could not name.
//
// The proof discriminates rather than printing a constant: the chain answering `true` for
// every value is the shape a broken one takes, so the second instance is a `boolean`, the
// one arm outside `U`, and its cell must print the MISS.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
type U = i32 | string
function mkU(): U | boolean { return "ab" }
function mkNotU(): U | boolean { return true }
// @@VALUE@@
mkU()
// @@TYPE@@
U | boolean
// @@PROOF@@
if v is U { print("yes") } else { print("no") }
// @@WANT@@
yes
// @@TEST@@
v is U
// @@HIT@@
print("yes")
// @@MISS@@
print("no")
// @@VALUE2@@
mkNotU()
// @@TYPE2@@
U | boolean
// @@PROOF2@@
if v is U { print("yes") } else { print("no") }
// @@WANT2@@
no
// @@SKIP@@
array_element: D1790 — an UN-ANNOTATED list literal of a union carrying an alias arm is check-clean invalid wasm at both seeds, with no `is` in the program at all
array_element_place: D1790, the same cell read back through its place
